      "hints": [
        "Find midpoint $(\\frac{15}{2}, \\frac{1}{2})$ and gradient $m = -\\frac{3}{5}$.",
        "Use perpendicular gradient $\\frac{5}{3}$ and form the line equation."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Find the midpoint $M$ of $AB$:\n$$M = \\left(\\frac{5 + 10}{2}, \\frac{2 + (-1)}{2}\\right) = \\left(\\frac{15}{2}, \\frac{1}{2}\\right)$$",
        "Calculate the gradient of $AB$:\n$$m_{AB} = \\frac{-1 - 2}{10 - 5} = -\\frac{3}{5}$$",
        "Determine the perpendicular gradient:\n$$m_\\perp = -\\frac{1}{m_{AB}} = \\frac{5}{3}$$",
        "Form the equation of the perpendicular bisector through $\\left(\\frac{15}{2}, \\frac{1}{2}\\right)$:\n$$y - \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{5}{3}\\left(x - \\frac{15}{2}\\right) \\implies y = \\frac{5}{3}x - 12 \\quad (\\text{or } 5x - 3y = 36)$$"
      ],
